	(text "The I/O pins are drawn in the module's pad order down each edge.\nPad numbers are Seeed's: 1-14 the edge castellations,\n   15-23 the small pads between them.\nThe 3V3 pin is an output: the module's own regulator\n   makes the board's +3V3 rail.  C6 is its bulk capacitor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 103.505 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9a570ba3-bae9-56a9-a2dc-c877b9d2b0c3")
	)
	(text "Each motor has three adjacent pads.  Any GPIO can carry any PWM,\n   so phases may be swapped in layout.\nNo PWM on D6 / D7 (UART0, active at boot).\nDRV_EN is on D3, which is quiet at boot; R3 keeps the drivers\n   off until firmware raises it.\nMn_INk and DRV_EN go to page 1.  All 20 GPIO are used."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8e761857-71c4-5f87-ba67-54ade4625a7b")
	)
